From: Francois Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: tag_rtl8_4: do not mark trapped link-local frames
 as forwarded

The RTL8372N driver (package/kernel/rtl837x) sets the switch's
reserved-multicast actions to trap 01:80:c2:00:00:00 and 02-0f (STP,
LACP, EAPOL, LLDP, ...) to the CPU, so the switch never forwards these
frames between its ports. The trapped frames are expected to carry an
RTL8373-family reason code (0x5f is predicted, nothing is measured
yet), not the 80 that rtl8_4_read_tag() takes for a trap, so the tagger
calls dsa_default_offload_fwd_mark() for them. Once the ingress port
offloads a bridge, such a frame is marked as forwarded by hardware
although the hardware forwarded it nowhere, and
nbp_switchdev_allowed_egress() then keeps the bridge from sending it to
the other ports of the switch.

That matters wherever the bridge forwards link-local frames itself:
BPDUs while STP is off, and the group_fwd_mask addresses (EAPOL, LLDP).
They still reach ports outside the switch, such as Wi-Fi, but no longer
the other LAN ports. Two STP switches on different LAN ports that are
also cabled to each other no longer hear each other's BPDUs through the
router, so neither blocks a port, and broadcasts loop through the
switch's hardware flooding at line rate.

Do what tag_brcm and tag_mxl862xx do: never mark a frame with a
link-local destination, whatever its REASON. The mac header still points
at the DA in both the rtl8_4 and the rtl8_4t receive paths. PAUSE
(01:80:c2:00:00:01), which the driver does not trap, is dropped by the
bridge in any case.

This is right only while the switch does trap these frames. A frame the
switch forwards as well as delivering it to the CPU would be sent a
second time by a bridge with STP off. That is possibly the case with
RTL8365MB, the other user of this tagger, which programs no
reserved-multicast actions. No qualcommbe image uses it, which is why
this is a target patch and not proposed upstream as it is.
---
--- a/net/dsa/tag_rtl8_4.c
+++ b/net/dsa/tag_rtl8_4.c
@@ -193,7 +193,12 @@ static int rtl8_4_read_tag(struct sk_buf
 		return -ENOENT;
 	}
 
-	if (reason != RTL8_4_REASON_TRAP)
+	/* The switch traps link-local frames to the CPU instead of forwarding
+	 * them, and need not report that as RTL8_4_REASON_TRAP: never mark
+	 * them, so that the bridge forwards them in software.
+	 */
+	if (reason != RTL8_4_REASON_TRAP &&
+	    !is_link_local_ether_addr(eth_hdr(skb)->h_dest))
 		dsa_default_offload_fwd_mark(skb);
 
 	return 0;
